  #line-at(56.88pt, 302.64pt, "ABSTRACT:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(126.226pt, 302.64pt, " Polyimide (PI) thin films are widely used in advanced technologies, yet accurate ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 330.24pt, "characterization of their thermal properties remains challenging, as evidenced by significant ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 357.84pt, "inconsistencies in reported data and an incomplete understanding of heat transfer mechanisms. In this ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 385.44pt, "study, we employ an optical Square-Pulsed Source (SPS) technique to simultaneously measure the ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 413.04pt, "in-plane and cross-plane thermal conductivities, as well as the volumetric heat capacity, of PI thin ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 440.64pt, "films. SPS is a pump-probe method that utilizes a square-wave-modulated pump laser to induce ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 468.24pt, "periodic heating and a probe laser to detect the thermoreflectance response. Thermal properties are ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 495.84pt, "extracted by analyzing amplitude signals across multiple modulation frequencies and laser spot sizes. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 523.44pt, "Measurements were conducted on both suspended commercial PI films and spin-coated PI films on ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 551.04pt, "fused silica substrates. The results show that spin-coated films exhibit higher cross-plane thermal ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 578.64pt, "conductivity and lower anisotropy compared to suspended films, which we attribute to differences in ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 606.24pt, "molecular orientation and substrate interactions. These findings provide new physical insights into ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 633.84pt, "anisotropic heat transport in polymer thin films and demonstrate the SPS technique as a robust tool ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 661.44pt, "for probing microscale thermal phenomena in soft materials.  ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 716.64pt, "KEYWORDS: Polyimide thin films, Anisotropic thermal conductivity, Heat capacity, Kapton films, ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 744.24pt, "Square-pulsed source (SPS) method")
]

