  #line-at(56.88pt, 68.16pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(74.88pt, 95.76pt, "Polyimide (PI) thin films are widely used in advanced applications such as microelectronics, ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 123.36pt, "aerospace engineering, and energy systems due to their exceptional thermal stability, chemical ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 150.96pt, "resistance, and mechanical strength [1–5]. These attributes make PI films ideal for high-temperature ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 178.56pt, "circuits, flexible electronics, and thermal insulation in spacecraft. However, as devices’ ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 206.16pt, "miniaturization and power densities continue to increase, effective thermal management has become ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 233.76pt, "critical, underscoring the need for accurate thermal property characterization to ensure reliable ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 261.36pt, "performance. ")
  #line-at(74.88pt, 288.96pt, "Thermal transport in PI thin films is inherently anisotropic, largely influenced by molecular ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 316.8pt, "alignment and processing conditions [6–9]. Typically, the in-plane thermal conductivity (")
