  #line-at(74.88pt, 458.4pt, "In summary, although the measured thermal conductivity and volumetric heat capacity vary ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 486pt, "among different types of PI films, the thermal anisotropy ratio generally lies within the range of 1.58 ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 513.6pt, "to 4. For spin-coated PI films, the measurement results are highly sensitive to the quality of the ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 541.2pt, "polyimide precursor solution and the thermal curing conditions. In this study, the spin-coated films ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 569.04pt, "demonstrated a distinct enhancement in ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(261.262pt, 569.04pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.4pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(267.883pt, 571.44pt, "\"")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.276pt, 569.04pt, " accompanied by a reduced thermal anisotropy ratio ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 596.88pt, "compared to the commercial PI films. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 624.48pt, "4. CONCLUSIONS  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(74.88pt, 652.08pt, "In this work, we employed the SPS method to characterize three commercial PI films and three ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 679.68pt, "spin-coated PI films on fused silica substrates. The obtained thermal conductivity, specific heat ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 707.28pt, "capacity, and thermal anisotropic ratio show good agreement with literature values, thereby ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 734.88pt, "establishing a novel approach for measuring similar polymer thin films. Notably, our methodology ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 762.48pt, "eliminates the need to use volumetric heat capacity as a predefined input parameter, a key advantage ")
]

